    "number": 36572,
    "state": "open",
    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "ipc: hold event loop references when using it in `CapnpProtocol`",
    "user": {
      "login": "xyzconstant",
      "id": 263061129,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOD63-iQ",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/263061129?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/xyzconstant",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/xyzconstant/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`EventLoop::loop()` exits when its reference count reaches zero. In `serve()` mode, the parent connection is the only reference keeping the loop running. Other `CapnpProtocol` methods called from threads not handling parent IPC requests do not hold their own references and therefore depend on the parent connection remaining alive.\r\n\r\nAdd `loopRef()` (code suggested by @ryanofsky in https://github.com/bitcoin-core/libmultiprocess/pull/376#discussion_r4268952676), which returns a new reference to the event loop or throws if the loop is not running or is shutting down, and use it in the methods that need the loop. Protect `m_loop` with a new `m_loop_mutex` to prevent `serve()` from destroying the loop while `loopRef()` is accessing it.",
    "labels": [
