      "tree": {
        "sha": "a383d06f4b6567d72e155e851656af42a85685c1",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/a383d06f4b6567d72e155e851656af42a85685c1"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree a383d06f4b6567d72e155e851656af42a85685c1\nparent 117c54d4c575aa19027b2227bb45dc60b63b3278\nauthor xyzconstant <263061129+xyzconstant@users.noreply.github.com> 1792371291 -0300\ncommitter xyzconstant <263061129+xyzconstant@users.noreply.github.com> 1794366306 -0300\n\nipc: hold event loop references when using it in CapnpProtocol\n\nEventLoop::loop() exits when its reference count reaches zero. In serve()\nmode, the parent connection is the only reference keeping the loop running.\nOther CapnpProtocol methods called from threads not handling parent IPC\nrequests do not hold their own references and therefore depend on the\nparent connection remaining alive.\n\nAdd loopRef(), which returns a new reference to the event loop or throws\nif the loop is not running or is shutting down, and use it in the methods\nthat need the loop. Protect m_loop with a new m_loop_mutex to prevent\nserve() from destroying the loop while loopRef() is accessing it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Ryan Ofsky <ryan@ofsky.org>\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niQHPBAABCAA5FiEEIbDHlvdH8seWa3oA61Yt6Z9Cs9EFAmrz22MbFIAAAAAABAAO\nbWFudTIsMi41KzEuMTIsMCwzAAoJEOtWLemfQrPR8lAL/1CgeXrB6YzBqHpsugBc\nRt2805XJYuhZl+lh2zfy0pXdrr5hPHmd54NT6ZoO4Cb0I2DWevFx6+2x5/AQQIVI\nhPOktjmEGHZyaS9Dbo4mxxh9aGewDqp3baVpMkXtfk/3W98qHwpLcktxIZnfrgPX\np7dNmcWrWCrl2O9dPmHTq6GH+QAOBahYWdsyVUiwQ6ankVT/OVeEw3g2IaRAW4Ud\nTRmjT0zRQ7WXXoM4ZITBhFQyCa7yPhw3pJOwLC8tVuXj64yweYoa08Uq2jCIXvTZ\nQL+6immECThpynO2xToUquE0jalhMzfLqymwDLMva+AjO7gd5ZdLFnyU9XH1rkNB\nWQAWF5KV2oDVhFc+YhBK4N10LFIJsPEj6Bp1lVz35jGt/Y+NmHK58v9xtucRFb/D\nnAJabsJRKijJSxQ/2+EfJ1ICfcNlGyD3UkvuvEEVO6stSuXQTPj1b6b8kfE1hbgl\nxyUcuVVXJDwbDaJAVvQDH8LJ2PbLt/lVb31MucRjfUOQ5A==\n=AJwj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
